- op: discuss  # 39d2
  at: '2026-08-28T06:38:52Z'  # 39d2
  by: agent  # 39d2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 39d2
  clock: 7  # 39d2
  nonce: 39d2  # 39d2
  message: "APPROVAL RECEIVED AND ACTED ON. Thank you -- and the delay is mine to own: the\napproval landed 2026-08-27T23:52Z and I carried it as still-blocked for a day.\nFix committed on jgstern-agent/fix/zamoh-manifest-zero-selection, going out via\nauto-pr per the \"without --gov\" grant.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED -- BOTH defects named in the description, not just the approved\ntwo-liner.\n\n(1) The empty-selection death. \"|| true\" on BOTH branches of\n_manifest_selected_tests. Both, because the marker-less else branch serves\nmanifests written before the sections existed, and a fix applied to one arm of\nan if/else is how a defect survives its own patch.\n\n(2) The header/body contradiction, which the approved patch did NOT cover. The\nunion now restates \"# Selected tests:\" from what it actually wrote, AFTER the\nexistence filter, and only ever as a correction -- a header carrying no count\nline does not gain one. I checked who reads that count before deciding it\nmattered: ci.yml:935 recomputes it from the body it is about to run, and the\npre-commit hook gates only on \"# Mode: full-suite\". So it was a manifest that\nLIED, not one that broke, and I am reporting it that way rather than claiming a\nlive CI failure I did not observe.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (this item's statement is about auto-pr's runtime\nbehaviour, so a proxy will not do). Replayed the filed repro against the REAL\ncommitted manifest (334 paths) and a REAL zero-selection regen, both arms under\nset -euo pipefail, old library from git show HEAD:\n  pre-fix:  exit 1, and NO OUTPUT FILE WRITTEN AT ALL -- the shell died inside\n            the function, which is exactly the \"nothing left behind\" shape.\n  post-fix: exit 0, all 334 committed paths preserved, header restated 0 -> 334.\nAll three tests the description asked for are in, plus four more:\n1657 passed across 96 affected files; mypy strict ratchet clean at 669.\n\nTHE FINDING THAT MATTERS MORE THAN EITHER PATCH. The test file already had\nthirteen cases over this exact function and every one of them passed, before\nand after. They sourced the library into a plain bash -c with errexit and\npipefail OFF, so the very status that kills auto-pr was discarded by the\nharness. A test that does not reproduce the caller shell options is not testing\nthe caller. The harness now sets set -euo pipefail BEFORE the source, exactly\nas auto-pr does on line 3; all thirteen still pass, so the hardening cost\nnothing and would have caught this on the day the guard landed.\n\nANALOGUE SWEEP (structural protocol). Swept scripts/auto-pr and\nscripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh for other pipelines terminating in grep under\nset -e: none. Checked the same shape in ci.yml -- its selected-tests pipeline\nends in tr, which exits 0, so it is safe even under errexit. One genuine\nanalogue found and NOT fixed here: ci.yml counts the manifest with\ngrep -c \"^packages/\" at lines 717, 773 and 1116 -- the identical path-prefix\nmistake that _manifest_test_count exists to have fixed on the auto-pr side,\nstill standing in CI reporting, where it reads 0 for any manifest of\nroot-level tests/... entries. It is echoed to the log only and gates nothing.\nFiling it separately rather than widening this PR.\n\nI will move this item to satisfied after the merge, not before."  # 39d2
