- op: discuss  # 2161
  at: '2026-08-28T06:59:02Z'  # 2161
  by: agent  # 2161
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2161
  clock: 9  # 2161
  nonce: '2161'  # 2161
  message: "SATISFIED. Merged as PR #599, dev fa65f2352f. Both clauses of the statement are\nverified on the MERGED tree, by behaviour rather than by proxy, with a control\nin the same run.\n\nTHE FULL CAUSAL CHAIN, EVERY LINK A REAL ARTIFACT (no hand-written fixtures):\n  1. TRIGGER. A docs-only commit (one line appended to docs/hypergumbo-spec.md\n     on a scratch branch), then smart-test --manifest. It writes:\n       # Reason: no test-relevant files changed (docs/config only)\n       # Selected tests: 0        (body: 0 paths)\n     So the population is real and the generator produces it, not just my\n     reading of the code.\n  2. THE DEATH. That genuine zero manifest and the real committed manifest\n     (334 paths) into the PRE-FIX library, under set -euo pipefail:\n       exit 1, and NO OUTPUT FILE WRITTEN AT ALL.\n     The shell died inside the function -- the \"nothing left behind\" shape the\n     description reports from the live ADR-0046 branch.\n  3. THE FIX. Same two inputs, merged library, same shell options:\n       exit 0, all 334 committed paths preserved, header restated 0 -> 334.\n  4. CONTROL, same run: identical non-empty inputs (334 in) must not move --\n     exit 0, 334 out, header 334. It does not move.\n\nCLAUSE 2 (declared count equals body count) is covered by 3 and 4 above and by\nfive new tests, including the case the union makes uniquely awkward: the count\nis taken AFTER the existence filter, and after the fail-safe fallback, so it\ndescribes what was actually written rather than what the filter would have left.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED: \"|| true\" on BOTH branches of _manifest_selected_tests (the\napproved patch), plus the count restatement the approved patch did not cover.\nThe restatement is only ever a correction -- a header with no count line does\nnot gain one.\n\nTHE HARNESS GAP IS THE REAL LESSON, and it is fixed too. This function already\nhad thirteen tests and every one passed before and after. They sourced the\nlibrary into a plain bash -c with errexit and pipefail OFF, so the very status\nthat kills auto-pr was discarded by the harness. The tests now set\nset -euo pipefail BEFORE the source, exactly as scripts/auto-pr:3 does; all\nthirteen still pass, and seven new cases pin the empty selection. Had the\nharness matched the caller, this would have been caught the day the guard\nlanded.\n\nWHAT I HAVE NOT OBSERVED, stated plainly: no real docs-only branch has yet gone\nthrough a full auto-pr run post-fix -- PR #599 itself touches code. The library\nstep that killed it is verified end to end with the generator's own output; the\nfield confirmation is the next docs-only PR, and no workaround is needed for it\n(AUTO_PR_SKIP_MANIFEST=1 can be retired).\n\nANALOGUE SWEEP: no other grep-terminated pipeline under set -e in\nscripts/auto-pr or scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh. ci.yml's selected-tests pipeline\nends in tr (exit 0), safe even under errexit. One genuine analogue found and\nfiled separately rather than widening this PR: ci.yml counts the manifest with\ngrep -c \"^packages/\" at lines 717, 773 and 1116, the same path-prefix mistake\n_manifest_test_count exists to have fixed, reading 0 for any manifest of\nroot-level tests/... entries. Diagnostic only -- it gates nothing."  # 2161
